# Use Cases

100 questions total. Even split (~17 per use case). Sorted by Normain mode. UC IDs are stable identifiers, not ordering.

**Uniqueness** = how much of this test exercises capabilities that aren't already covered by another use case in the benchmark. Higher = more distinctive contribution to total coverage. Subjective estimate.

| # | Use case | Mode | Persona | Scenario | Question types | # docs | # questions | Uniqueness | What it tests |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 01 | Due diligence financial review | Simple | PE / corp dev analyst reviewing a target | Verify financials, spot red flags, cross-check numbers between annual report, proxy, and Excel model | Numerical calc; cross-doc (10-K vs proxy); Excel step-by-step logic; reasoning on covenants/warning signs | 6 | 17 | **35%** — Excel step-by-step logic is unique; numerical + cross-doc overlap with UC02/UC03/UC04 | Numeric extraction + cross-doc consistency + chained reasoning |
| 06 | Multimodal evidence extraction | Simple | Advisory / forensic analyst | Single mixed-format corpus; varied Qs pull facts from scans, photos, charts, handwriting | OCR-grade text from scans; handwriting recognition; image-only chart interpretation; cross-modal reconciliation | 4 | 16 | **90%** — only test covering scanned, handwritten, image-only formats; minimal overlap with anything else | Format coverage — exposes tools that can't ingest non-text inputs |
| 02 | ESG / sustainability audit | Repeat | Sustainability lead prepping CSRD, or auditor | Same Qs across multiple companies' sustainability reports → comparison table | Exhaustive search; numerical aggregation; multi-doc cross-reference (report vs framework) | 4 | 17 | **35%** — framework-vs-disclosure alignment is the unique angle; exhaustive + numerical + cross-doc all duplicated elsewhere | Long-doc exhaustive extraction + framework alignment |
| 04 | Contract clause sweep | Repeat | Legal ops / M&A counsel | Same clause-finding Qs across each contract in a bundle → per-contract table | Exhaustive (find every X); classification; clause-level citation fidelity | ~12 | 17 | **55%** — clause-level citation fidelity at scale is the differentiator; exhaustive search overlaps UC02/UC05 | Exhaustive search across many docs + accurate clause-level citation |
| 03 | Regulatory-vs-policy gap check | Spreadsheet | GRC / internal audit | Each row = one obligation from the regulation; columns assess policy coverage with citations | Cross-doc (reg vs policy); exhaustive requirements enumeration; classification; reasoning on partial coverage | 6 | 17 | **60%** — per-obligation structured enumeration unique; cross-doc + exhaustive overlap others | Cross-doc reasoning + exhaustiveness + citation fidelity |
| 05 | Vendor / supplier risk matrix | Spreadsheet | GRC / vendor management / TPRM lead | Each row = one vendor; columns score risk dimensions (data handling, breach history, cert status, sub-processor exposure) using vendor's SOC2 + public disclosures + ToS | Cross-doc per vendor; classification (risk tier); per-column varied questions; citation across short security docs | ~15 | 16 | **65%** — vendor TPRM scenario unrepresented elsewhere; partial overlap with UC03 on Spreadsheet mode and UC04 on legal-doc parsing | Per-row varied prompting + cross-doc per entity + risk classification |

